  "generated_text": "1. **Simplify the Expression:**\n   \\[\n   \\prod_{k=0}^{n-1} \\left( \\left( 1 + e^{2 \\pi i k / n} \\right)^n + 1 \\right)\n   \\]\n   Notice that:\n   \\[\n   \\left( 1 + e^{2 \\pi i k / n} \\right)^n = e^{2 \\pi i k}\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\left( 1 + e^{2 \\pi i k / n} \\right)^n + 1 = e^{2 \\pi i k} + 1\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   e^{2 \\pi i k} + 1 = 1 + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Analyze the Product:**\n   Since each term in the product is 2, the product is simply $2^n$. Therefore, the product is never zero for any $n$.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   The product is never zero, so there are no integers $n$ for which the product is zero.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
